{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Upon the thumb.</b> Its meaning is known from its source. Now, the one purified from tzara'at, which is on the body, is like the priest at his ordination, for sin is like tzara'at in the soul. The thumb is the place of joining and is the root of all deeds, and the right side on account of the power of the right side. And the ear — male, to hear — as He commanded."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra here interprets the word תנוך ('earlobe') as related to אזן ('ear'), deriving 'to hear' from it; the structure 'the thumb… and the ear… as He commanded' maps onto the three body parts (thumb, toe, ear) in the verse, with each given symbolic rationale."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:07.028206600Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}